body: |-
  RESTART HERE. Branch conductor-revival-phase0 (commits → 1a3b17c1; history → h0472; NOT merged — Matt merges/publishes himself). Launch: open packages/conductor/build/Conductor.app, ⌘⇧A. ⌘=/⌘- adjusts cockpit font.

  SHIPPED THIS WAVE (on top of THE BRIDGE fleet cockpit): the two-pronged "reduce the walls of text" feature —
  1. CONCISION: per-session system prompt via --append-system-prompt (Scholar's bridgeConventions: lead-with-answer, one-rec, ~6 lines then stop-or-block, caveats exempt). SessionPrompt.swift.
  2. DECISIONS: FencedBlockParser (streaming-safe, emit only on closing fence) extracts ```conductor-decision; AtriumDecisionCard renders inline (radio/checkbox/Other, composer never locks); pick → amber→teal → "✓ you chose X"; answer = normal text turn via send(). Pending decision → noteNeedsHuman() → derivedStatus.awaitingYou (FIRST-CLASS needs-you amber, pages even active session).
  3. VISUALS / THE LIGHTBOX: ```conductor-visual + ```mermaid + ```svg; AtriumVisualCanvas right slide-out OVER the still-mounted CHORUS rail; flow→MermaidWebView (sandboxed, VENDORED OFFLINE mermaid.min.js in Conductor_Conductor.bundle), comparison→native table; ▸ launcher (no auto-open).
  4. Larger + ⌘=/⌘--adjustable cockpit type scale (@AppStorage atriumFontScale).

  VERIFIED FACTS (don't re-derive): AskUserQuestion surfaces as a clean tool_use but is unanswerable headless (auto-dismisses) → use the fenced-block convention; --append-system-prompt (NOT --system-prompt, which strips default tools). Plus prior facts (control_request interrupt, TaskStop, task_type local_agent/local_bash + tool_use_id correlation, macOS LSUIElement/TCC/PATH/NSTextView gotchas) — see L-2026-06-16-ascend-091000-001.

  DISCIPLINE: Swift ecosystem agent owns ALL Conductor Swift. Debug via ~/.paradigm/conductor/atrium transcripts (READ them). Run the bundled .app. NO blockquotes (global rule). Be concise (we're literally building the cure for walls of text).

  ON RESTART: Matt is testing + will keep working on THIS feature wave. Likely next: polish (decision-card feel, LIGHTBOX+CHORUS side-by-side option) or the v2 backlog.

  OPEN v2 / backlog: wireframe + diff visual kinds; hover-option↔diagram highlight binding (Mika nicety); animations; raw-svg render; LIGHTBOX+CHORUS side-by-side (today LIGHTBOX overlays); cockpit history/log viewer over the atrium transcripts (T-2026-06-17-001). Pre-existing: merge conductor-revival-phase0; the on-call v2 (UserNotifications/voice page-back, session persistence via --resume).
